{"name":"Ibis Mouse","hex":"#e4d2d8","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"ibis","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Any of various long-legged wading birds in the family Threskiornithidae, having long downcurved bills used to probe the mud for prey such as crustaceans."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/ibis"},{"term":"mouse","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Any mammal of the many rodent families (especially Muridae) that have a small body and a long tail.","Such a rodent that is of the genus Mus."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To move cautiously or furtively, in the manner of a mouse (the rodent) (frequently used in the phrasal verb to mouse around).","To hunt or catch mice (the rodents), usually of cats. .mw-parser-output .defdate{font-size:smaller}"]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/mouse"}],"entries":[{"title":"Ibis","blocks":[{"text":"The ibis are a group of long-legged wading birds in the family Threskiornithidae that inhabit wetlands, forests and plains. \"Ibis\" derives from the Latin and Ancient Greek word for this group of birds. It also occurs in the scientific name of the western cattle egret mistakenly identified in 1757 as being the sacred ibis."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c1/Black-headed_Ibis_%28Threskiornis_melanocephalus%29.jpg/330px-Black-headed_Ibis_%28Threskiornis_melanocephalus%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ibis","wikidata":"Q193833"},{"title":"Mouse","blocks":[{"text":"A mouse is a small rodent, characteristically known to have a pointed snout, small rounded ears, a body-length scaly tail, and a high breeding rate. The best known mouse species is the common house mouse. Mice are widely available as pets, but not as popular as some other rodents. In some places, certain kinds of field mice are locally common. They are known to invade homes for food and shelter."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/0d/%D0%9C%D1%8B%D1%88%D1%8C_2.jpg/330px-%D0%9C%D1%8B%D1%88%D1%8C_2.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Mouse","wikidata":"Q2751034"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/9f/N190_w1150.jpg/500px-N190_w1150.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/9f/N190_w1150.jpg/1280px-N190_w1150.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/9f/N190_w1150.jpg/500px-N190_w1150.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Ibises illustration, c. 1835–1840","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AN190_w1150.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/50/American_White_IbisII.jpg/500px-American_White_IbisII.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/50/American_White_IbisII.jpg/500px-American_White_IbisII.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AAmerican_White_IbisII.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/fc/Black-faced_ibis_%28Theristicus_melanopis%29_Tricao.jpg/500px-Black-faced_ibis_%28Theristicus_melanopis%29_Tricao.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/fc/Black-faced_ibis_%28Theristicus_melanopis%29_Tricao.jpg/1280px-Black-faced_ibis_%28Theristicus_melanopis%29_Tricao.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/fc/Black-faced_ibis_%28Theristicus_me